    <exercise>
        <introduction>
            <p>
                Math Ninjas is a local community program that offers Saturday
                martial arts classes for children ages 8 to 12 over the course
                of 6 months.
                They recruit from the community and estimate that 10% of the
                "not-enrolled," eligible new students enroll at the beginning of
                each month.
                Children begin in "white belt" status, and as each month passes,
                the top 35% of the white belt class moves to the "yellow belt"
                status, but 25% of the class drops out (and is considered to
                return to a general, "not-enrolled" population).
                After the end of 1 month in yellow belt status, 40% of the
                students remain in the program (in the same status) but the rest
                drop out of the program.
                Students who drop out of the classes and decide to re-enroll can
                only begin again as white belt students.
            </p>
        </introduction>

        <task>
            <statement>
                <p>
                    Set up a transition matrix for enrollment in the Math Ninjas
                    program.
                    You can use Python here.
                </p>
            </statement>
        </task>

        <task>
            <statement>
                <p>
                    The community has 500 children who are 8 to 12 years old.
                    How many white belt students are in the class at the
                    beginning of the program (time 0)?
                    Approximately how many white belt and yellow belt students
                    are in the class at the beginning of the second month of the
                    program?
                    You can use python here as well.
                </p>
            </statement>
        </task>

        <task>
            <statement>
                <p>
                    Use python to find the steady-state vector for your
                    Transition Probability Matrix.
                </p>
            </statement>
        </task>

        <task>
            <statement>
                <p>
                    The classes last 6 months.
                    Show the 6th month trajectory in a plot.
                    Recall that the 0th probability vector is before the program
                    starts, and make sure you include enough time steps to show
                    the value at the END of 6 months of the program.
                </p>
            </statement>
        </task>

        <task>
            <statement>
                <p>
                    How does your end value compare to your steady-state vector?
                    (Recall, you may need to turn something into probabilities.)
                </p>
            </statement>
        </task>

        <task>
            <statement>
                <p>
                    How can you improve this model?
                </p>
            </statement>
        </task>
    </exercise>
</worksheet>